WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.880
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:12.240
Today we are going to see what happens if&nbsp;
we unleash an AI to watch Minecraft videos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.960
and then, ask this AI to play&nbsp;
it. And the big question is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:23.200
can it play as well as we, humans do?&nbsp;
Well, you’ll get your answer today!

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:30.560
This is OpenAI’s project, which is not to be&nbsp;
confused with NVIDIA’s similar project called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:37.120
MineDojo. So, what was that? That&nbsp;
was an AI project that watched a ton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:44.080
of Youtube tutorial videos on Minecraft.&nbsp;
Minecraft is an open world sandbox game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:50.560
one of the most played games in the world, and&nbsp;
this is a true sandbox, which means that you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:58.880
can do whatever you wish. You create the story of&nbsp;
this game. Gather raw materials, build something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:08.080
explore, or don’t, it’s all up to you. This is&nbsp;
a sandbox game, and your story after all. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:15.760
what could NVIDIA’s AI do after watching&nbsp;
these tutorial videos? Well, a great deal.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:22.320
For instance, we could even use natural&nbsp;
language and ask it to explore an ocean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:28.000
monument. I really liked this one because&nbsp;
the word “explore” is sufficiently vague&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:35.600
and open ended. A human understands what exploring&nbsp;
means, but does the AI understand it too?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:43.840
Well, as you see, it does! Amazing. It could&nbsp;
also encircle these llamas with a fence.&nbsp;

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:50.160
Or, it could also be dropped into&nbsp;
an arena with an Ender Dragon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.760
the final boss of the game, if you will. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.760 --> 00:02:00.800
look, this is a very limited setting for this&nbsp;
task as the dragon is not charging at the AI.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:06.720
But at the very least, NVIDIA’s AI&nbsp;
understood what fighting meant in this game.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:14.880
Now, I said the following, quoting: “Starting&nbsp;
this game from scratch and building up everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:21.520
to defeat such a dragon takes a long time&nbsp;
horizon, and will be an excellent benchmark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:27.840
for the next AI one more paper down the line.&nbsp;
I’d love to see it perform this start to end.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:33.200
Make sure to subscribe, if such a paper&nbsp;
appears, I’ll be here to show it to you.”

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:42.080
And I thought, maybe a year or two later there&nbsp;
will be some activity here. And now, hold on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:48.400
to your papers, because OpenAI’s scientists&nbsp;
are here with their own spin of this project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:55.600
not one year later, but just one week&nbsp;
later. Wow! And, with this paper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:01.840
I also got what I was looking for, which is&nbsp;
an AI that understands longer time horizons.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:10.000
They make a huge claim. They say that this is&nbsp;
the first AI that is capable of crafting Diamond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:17.680
tools. That is very ambitious. Can that really&nbsp;
be? Well, I say that I will believe it when I see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:25.680
it. Do you see this long sequence of subtasks?&nbsp;
We need to do all this correctly and in order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:33.920
to be able to perform that. This takes up to 24000&nbsp;
actions and 20 minutes even for a human player.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:43.200
So, let’s see if the AI is also up for the task!&nbsp;
It starts chopping wood right away, then, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:53.760
planks are coming along. Later, it starts mining,&nbsp;
finds iron ore, crafts a furnace, starts smelting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.760 --> 00:04:00.800
and at this point I am starting to think that it&nbsp;
might make it. That would be absolutely amazing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:08.640
However, we still need some diamonds. Can&nbsp;
it find some diamonds? It takes a while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:16.640
and…oh my, got ‘em! And from then on, we have&nbsp;
established that this is a smart AI, so from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:24.720
here on out, this is a piece of cake. There&nbsp;
we go. I can’t believe it. A diamond pickaxe.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:33.440
And here is my other favorite, it can also perform&nbsp;
pillar jumps. This is a cool technique where we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:42.080
jump, and while mid-air, we quickly put a block&nbsp;
below us, and tadaa. We are now standing a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:49.040
higher. If we do this over and over again, we will&nbsp;
be able to reach places that otherwise would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:54.640
way out of reach. And the AI&nbsp;
learned this too. How cool is that?

00:04:55.280 --> 00:05:01.520
While we are looking at what else it is capable&nbsp;
of, I would like to bring up one more remarkable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:08.400
thing here. Here goes: it learns from unlabeled&nbsp;
videos. In other words, this means that the AI is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:15.680
not told what these videos are about, it is just&nbsp;
allowed to watch them and find out for itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:22.320
And to be able to learn this much information&nbsp;
from this kind of unlabeled data just is an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:28.560
incredible sign for future projects to come.&nbsp;
You see, playing Minecraft well is great,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:35.440
but this is an AI that can learn new things&nbsp;
from unstructured data. In the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:42.320
these agents will be able to perform more general,&nbsp;
non-gaming related tasks. What a time to be alive!

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:49.600
For instance, the amazing DeepMind lab is&nbsp;
already walking this path. First they wrote an AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:57.520
that could learn to play Chess, Go, and Starcraft&nbsp;
2, and then, they used a similar system to solve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:03.760
protein folding. Now, make no mistake, the&nbsp;
protein folding system is not exactly the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:08.720
same system as the chess AI, but&nbsp;
they share a few building blocks.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:16.000
And here, having two amazing Minecraft AIs&nbsp;
appear within a week of each other is a true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.640
testament to how quickly projects&nbsp;
are coming along in AI research.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:26.960
So, let’s apply the first Law of Papers&nbsp;
- what do you think this will be capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:30.880
of one more paper down the line?&nbsp;
Let me know in the comments below!

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:20.960
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

